n reaches the store deletion effect. Separately, this matches the accepted original policy, which allows an active space member to delete their own membership to leave. This is a source-visible authorization result, not a claim that the deployment or downstream store operation necessarily succeeds. Only the declared entry and fixed source ranges were assessed; source discovery is not-tested, so no repository-wide or deployment conclusion is made.","facts":[{"id":"self-entry","kind":"entry","statement":"DeleteSpaceMember is the assessed handler entry.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":740,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"self-identity-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"The handler obtains the authenticated current user before resolving the requested space-member resource.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":741,"endLine":746}]},{"id":"self-resource-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"Resource resolution binds the selected space, caller membership, target user, and target membership, and requires the target membership to be active.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":632,"endLine":662}]},{"id":"self-active-condition","kind":"condition","statement":"Active membership is defined by the active admin or active user roles, and resource resolution rejects a non-active target membership.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-b6a6c6968b02e733","startLine":64,"endLine":66},{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":651,"endLine":661}]},{"id":"self-identity-control","kind":"control","statement":"The handler identifies a self-target by comparing targetUser.ID with currentUser.ID; the administrator check is only executed when that comparison is false.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-43957c8318fc22f6","startLine":750,"endLine":755}]},{"id":"self-protected-effect","kind":"effect","statement":"After the self-target path bypasses the administrator-only check, the handler calls store deletion and publishes the spac